---

<ChronicleLayout meta={meta}>
  <ArticleHeader
    route={['Argentina', 'Buenos Aires', 'South America']}
    label="Guide · Ten Experiences"
    title="Best Things to Do in Buenos Aires"
    standfirst="Buenos Aires works through contrast: civic grandeur, theatre and books, Recoleta’s cultural institutions, San Telmo’s market streets, Puerto Madero’s docks, La Boca’s football-and-port identity and Palermo’s parks."
    stats={[
      { num: '10', label: 'Experiences' },
      { num: '5', label: 'Nights' },
      { num: '6', label: 'City areas' },
      { num: '1', label: 'First visit' },
    ]}
  />

  <div class="post-body">
    <div class="opening-prose">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="drop-cap">
          Buenos Aires did not reveal itself through one landmark. It arrived in sections:
          the civic scale of Plaza de Mayo, the Obelisk and Teatro Colón; the quieter
          concentration of books, museums and Recoleta; then markets, waterfront buildings,
          football streets and the green edge of Palermo.
        </p>
        <p>
          The city is easier to understand by moving between these worlds than by chasing
          one signature monument. Plaza de Mayo explains the political centre. Avenida 9 de
          Julio shows what modern Buenos Aires did to its own scale. Recoleta turns towards
          museums, monuments and the city’s grander cultural institutions, while San Telmo
          keeps older streets, market life and tango history close to the surface. Puerto
          Madero rewrites the waterfront. La Boca joins port history to football. Palermo
          finally gives the city room to loosen into parks and longer walks.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a discovery guide rather than a day-by-day itinerary. The recommendations
          come from the places that shaped a first visit during the September–October 2026
          stay, expanded with the historical and cultural context that makes each stop worth
          choosing. The traveller does not need to complete every district to understand the
          argument. The useful question is which change of character deserves the next part
          of the day.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

